00:44:06,562 --> 00:44:09,385
Is there anything you regret about what you did on that day?
关于那一天你所做的事情，有什么遗憾吗？

617
00:44:10,647 --> 00:44:13,909
I had nothing to do with that other than they asked me to make a speech.
我与此无关，除了他们让我发表演讲。

618
00:44:14,109 --> 00:44:15,250
I showed up for a speech.
我去发表了演讲。

619
00:44:15,310 --> 00:44:16,751
I said, I think it's going to be big.
我说，我认为这将会很盛大。

620
00:44:17,211 --> 00:44:23,535
I went to Nancy Pelosi and the mayor of Washington, D.C., and the mayor put it back in writing, as you know.
我去找南希·佩洛西和华盛顿特区的市长，市长如你所知，将其写了下来。

621
00:44:24,236 --> 00:44:28,658
I said, you know, this is going to be a very big rally or whatever you want to call it.
我说，你知道，这将会是一个非常大的集会，或者你想称之为其他什么。

622
00:44:29,039 --> 00:44:30,579
And again, it wasn't done by me.
而且，这不是我做的。

623
00:44:30,599 --> 00:44:31,400
It was done by others.
这是别人做的。

624
00:44:31,820 --> 00:44:35,803
I said, I'd like to give you 10,000 National Guard or soldiers.
我说，我想给你们提供1万名国民警卫队或士兵。

625
00:44:36,383 --> 00:44:37,283
They rejected me.
他们拒绝了我。

626
00:44:37,343 --> 00:44:39,004
Nancy Pelosi rejected me.
南希·佩洛西拒绝了我。

627
00:44:39,084 --> 00:44:40,725
It was just two weeks ago.
就在两周前。

628
00:44:40,785 --> 00:44:45,027
Her daughter has a tape of her saying she is fully responsible for what happened.
她的女儿有一段录像，录像中她说她对发生的事情完全负责。

629
00:44:45,347 --> 00:44:46,387
They want to get rid of that tape.
他们想要销毁那段录像。

630
00:44:47,247 --> 00:44:51,849
It would have never happened if Nancy Pelosi and the mayor of Washington did their jobs.
如果南希·佩洛西和华盛顿市长履行了他们的职责，这一切都不会发生。

631
00:44:52,290 --> 00:44:54,030
I wasn't responsible for security.
我并不负责安全。

632
00:44:54,370 --> 00:44:56,291
Nancy Pelosi was responsible.
南希·佩洛西负责。

633
00:44:56,531 --> 00:44:57,512
She didn't do her job.
她没有尽到自己的职责。

634
00:44:57,772 --> 00:45:00,893
The question was about you as president, not about former Speaker Pelosi.
问题是关于你作为总统的，而不是前议长佩洛西的。

635
00:45:00,933 --> 00:45:02,794
But I do want Vice President Harris to respond here.
但我确实希望哈里斯副总统在这里做出回应。

636
00:45:04,787 --> 00:45:06,507
I was at the Capitol on January 6th.
我在1月6日那天在国会大厦。

637
00:45:07,328 --> 00:45:09,548
I was the vice president-elect.
我当时是当选副总统。

638
00:45:09,608 --> 00:45:11,328
I was also an acting senator.
我也是一名代理参议员。

639
00:45:11,609 --> 00:45:12,069
I was there.
我在那里。

640
00:45:13,049 --> 00:45:25,532
And on that day, the President of the United States incited a violent mob to attack our nation's Capitol, to desecrate our nation's Capitol.
在那一天，美国总统煽动了一群暴徒攻击我们国家的国会大厦，亵渎了我们国家的国会大厦。

641
00:45:25,692 --> 00:45:30,813
On that day, 140 law enforcement officers were injured, and some died.
在那一天，140名执法人员受伤，还有一些人丧生。

642
00:45:32,017 --> 00:45:38,940
And understand, the former president has been indicted and impeached for exactly that reason.
请理解，前总统正是因为这个原因被起诉和弹劾。

643
00:45:39,801 --> 00:45:42,122
But this is not an isolated situation.
但这并不是孤立的事件。

644
00:45:42,782 --> 00:45:52,527
Let's remember Charlottesville, where there was a mob of people carrying tiki torches, spewing anti-Semitic hate.
让我们记住夏洛茨维尔，当时有一群人举着火把，散布反犹太主义的仇恨。

645
00:45:53,667 --> 00:45:56,749
And what did the president then at the time say?
那么当时的总统说了什么呢？

646
00:45:56,769 --> 00:45:59,150
There were fine people on each side.
两边都有很优秀的人。

647
00:45:59,990 --> 00:46:00,731
Let's remember.
让我们记住。

648
00:46:01,738 --> 00:46:09,708
that when it came to the Proud Boys, a militia, the president said, the former president said, stand back and stand by.
当谈到骄傲男孩这个民兵组织时，前总统说，退后并待命。

649
00:46:10,770 --> 00:46:18,019
So for everyone watching who remembers what January 6th was, I say we don't have to go back.
所以对于所有观看的人，记得1月6日是什么，我说我们不必回头。

650
00:46:19,099 --> 00:46:20,060
Let's not go back.
让我们不要回头。

651
00:46:20,100 --> 00:46:21,181
We're not going back.
我们不会回头。

652
00:46:21,542 --> 00:46:23,163
It's time to turn the page.
是时候翻开新的一页了。

653
00:46:24,104 --> 00:46:40,041
And if that was a bridge too far for you, well, there is a place in our campaign for you to stand for country, to stand for our democracy, to stand for rule of law, and to end the chaos
如果这对你来说是一个过于严苛的要求，那么在我们的竞选中有一个地方可以让你为国家而站立，为我们的民主而站立，为法治而站立，结束混乱

654
00:46:41,195 --> 00:46:49,079
and to end the approach that is about attacking the foundations of our democracy, because you don't like the outcome.
并结束那种攻击我们民主基础的方法，因为你不喜欢结果。

655
00:46:49,439 --> 00:46:51,480
And be clear on that point.
对此要明确。

656
00:46:51,900 --> 00:47:00,564
Donald Trump, the candidate, has said in this election there will be a bloodbath if this and the outcome of this election is not to his liking.
唐纳德·特朗普，作为候选人，在这次选举中表示，如果这次选举的结果不符合他的意愿，将会是一场血腥的屠杀。

657
00:47:01,874 --> 00:47:03,215
Let's turn the page on this.
让我们翻开新的一页。

658
00:47:03,495 --> 00:47:04,476
Let's not go back.
让我们不要回头。

659
00:47:04,996 --> 00:47:10,599
Let's chart a course for the future and not go backwards to the past.
让我们为未来制定一个方向，而不是倒退到过去。

660
00:47:10,979 --> 00:47:11,980
Let me just follow up here.
让我在这里补充一下。

661
00:47:13,160 --> 00:47:19,104
It was a different term, and it was a term that related to energy, because they have destroyed our energy business.
这是一个不同的任期，涉及到能源，因为他们摧毁了我们的能源产业。

662
00:47:19,144 --> 00:47:20,385
That was where Bloodbath was.
那就是“血腥屠杀”的地方。

663
00:47:20,745 --> 00:47:24,847
Also, on Charlottesville, that story has been, as you would say, debunked.
此外，关于夏洛茨维尔，那则故事已经被你们称之为揭穿了。

664
00:47:25,327 --> 00:47:26,268
Laura Ingram,
劳拉·英格拉姆，

665
00:47:26,508 --> 00:47:30,672
Sean Hannity, Jesse, all of these people, they covered it.
肖恩·汉尼蒂，杰西，所有这些人，他们都进行了报道。

666
00:47:30,953 --> 00:47:33,976
If they go an extra sentence, they will see it was perfect.
如果他们多说一句话，他们会发现这一切是完美的。

667
00:47:34,356 --> 00:47:40,062
It was debunked in almost every newspaper, but they still bring it up, just like they bring 2025 up.
几乎所有的报纸都揭穿了这一点，但他们仍然提起，就像他们提起2025一样。

668
00:47:40,443 --> 00:47:41,604
They bring all of this stuff up.
他们提起所有这些事情。

669
00:47:41,884 --> 00:47:44,246
I ask you this, you talk about the Capitol.
我问你们，你们谈论国会大厦。

670
00:47:45,067 --> 00:47:49,749
Why are we allowing these millions of people to come through on the southern border?
为什么我们允许这些数百万人通过南部边界进入？

671
00:47:49,769 --> 00:47:51,050
How come she's not doing anything?
她为什么不采取任何行动？

672
00:47:51,310 --> 00:47:54,031
And I'll tell you what I would do, and I would be very proud to do it.
我告诉你我会怎么做，我会很自豪地去做。

673
00:47:54,571 --> 00:47:57,493
I would say we would both leave this debate right now.
我会说我们两个现在就离开这个辩论。

674
00:47:58,093 --> 00:47:59,394
I'd like to see her go down
我想看看她去

675
00:48:00,194 --> 00:48:01,394
to Washington D.C.
华盛顿特区。

676
00:48:01,454 --> 00:48:09,076
during this debate, because we're wasting a lot of time, go down to, because she's been so bad, it's so ridiculous, go down to Washington D.C.
在这个辩论期间，因为我们浪费了很多时间，去吧，因为她表现得太糟糕，太荒谬，去华盛顿特区。

677
00:48:09,356 --> 00:48:11,817
and let her sign a bill to close up the border.
让她签署一项关闭边界的法案。

678
00:48:12,077 --> 00:48:13,617
Because they have the right to do it.
因为他们有权这样做。

679
00:48:13,657 --> 00:48:14,578
They don't need bills.
他们不需要法案。

680
00:48:14,938 --> 00:48:15,918
They have the right to do it.
他们有权这样做。

681
00:48:15,938 --> 00:48:23,320
The President of the United States, you'll get him out of bed, you'll wake him up at 4 o'clock in the afternoon, you'll say, come on, come on down to the office, let's sign a bill.
美国总统，你把他叫起床，你在下午四点把他叫醒，你会说，来吧，来办公室，让我们签署一项法案。

682
00:48:23,860 --> 00:48:30,324
If he signs a bill that the border is closed, all he has to do is say it to the border patrol, who are phenomenal.
如果他签署一项关闭边界的法案，他所需要做的就是告诉边境巡逻队，他们非常出色。

683
00:48:30,764 --> 00:48:33,046
If they do that, the border is closed.
如果他们这样做，边界就关闭了。

684
00:48:33,086 --> 00:48:36,328
Those people are killing many people, unlike J6.
那些人正在杀死很多人，不像J6。

685
00:48:36,348 --> 00:48:37,569
We talked immigration here tonight.
我们今晚谈论移民。

686
00:48:37,609 --> 00:48:44,393
I do want to focus on this next issue to both of you, because it really brings us, this into focus, truth in these times that we're living in.
我确实想关注下一个问题，因为这真的让我们聚焦在我们生活的这个时代的真相上。

687
00:48:45,073 --> 00:48:53,395
Mr. President, for three and a half years after you lost the 2020 election, you repeatedly falsely claimed that you won, many times saying you won in a landslide.
总统先生，在你失去2020年选举后的三年半里，你多次错误地声称你赢了，很多次说你是以压倒性胜利获胜的。

688
00:48:53,875 --> 00:49:01,956
In the past couple of weeks leading up to this debate, you have said, quote, you lost by a whisker, that you, quote, didn't quite make it, that you came up a little bit short.
在这次辩论前的几周里，你说过，你以微弱差距输掉，称你“没能成功”，你有点落后。

689
00:49:02,476 --> 00:49:02,996
I said that?
我说过吗？

690
00:49:03,216 --> 00:49:05,257
Are you now acknowledging that you lost in 2020?
你现在承认你在2020年输了？

691
00:49:05,317 --> 00:49:06,877
No, I don't acknowledge that at all.
不，我根本不承认这一点

692
00:49:06,897 --> 00:49:07,317
But you did say that.
但你确实说过。

693
00:49:07,337 --> 00:49:08,217
I said that sarcastically.
我那是讽刺地说的。

694
00:49:08,257 --> 00:49:08,717
You know that.
你知道的。

695
00:49:09,177 --> 00:49:10,718
We said, oh, we lost by a whisker.
我们说，哦，我们差一点就输了。

696
00:49:10,978 --> 00:49:12,238
That was said sarcastically.
那是讽刺地说的。

697
00:49:13,678 --> 00:49:14,618
There's so much proof.
有很多证据。

698
00:49:14,818 --> 00:49:16,159
All you have to do is look at it.
你只需要看看就知道。

699
00:49:16,379 --> 00:49:19,420
And they should have sent it back to the legislatures for approval.
他们应该把它送回立法机构批准。

700
00:49:19,820 --> 00:49:24,281
I got almost 75 million votes, the most votes any sitting president has ever gotten.
我得到了近7500万票，这是任何现任总统获得的最多选票。

701
00:49:24,321 --> 00:49:28,963
I was told if I got 63, which was what I got in 2016, you can't be beaten.
我被告知如果我得到63万票（就是我在2016年得到的），你就无法被击败。

702
00:49:29,783 --> 00:49:33,746
The election people should never be thinking about an election is fraudulent.
选举人员绝不应该认为选举是欺诈的。

703
00:49:33,766 --> 00:49:34,607
We need two things.
我们需要两件事。

704
00:49:34,667 --> 00:49:37,529
We need walls We need and we have to have it.
我们需要墙，我们必须有它。

705
00:49:37,809 --> 00:49:45,054
We have to have borders and we have to have good elections Our elections are bad and a lot of these illegal immigrants coming in.
我们必须有边界，我们必须有良好的选举。我们的选举很糟糕，很多非法移民进来。

706
00:49:45,314 --> 00:49:46,816
They're trying to get them to vote.
他们试图让他们投票。

707
00:49:46,876 --> 00:49:55,662
They can't even speak English They don't even know what country they're in practically and these people are trying to get them to vote and that's why they're allowing Them to come into our country
他们甚至不会说英语，几乎不知道自己在哪个国家，这些人试图让他们投票，这就是为什么他们允许他们进入我们的国家。

708
00:49:55,862 --> 00:49:57,644
You should watch all of these pieces of video.
你应该看看所有这些视频片段。

709
00:49:58,405 --> 00:49:59,726
I didn't detect the sarcasm.
我没有察觉到讽刺。

710
00:49:59,766 --> 00:50:00,547
Lost by a whisker.
差一点就输了。

711
00:50:00,567 --> 00:50:01,428
We didn't quite make it.
我们没能成功。

712
00:50:01,948 --> 00:50:08,675
And we should just point out here, as clarification, and you know this, you and your allies, 60 cases in front of many judges, many of them Republican, and said there was no widespread fraud.
我们应该在这里指出，作为澄清，而你知道的，你和你的盟友，60个案件在许多法官面前，其中许多是共和党人，他们说没有广泛的欺诈。

713
00:50:08,695 --> 00:50:09,256
No judge looked at it.
没有法官审视过。

714
00:50:09,276 --> 00:50:10,517
They said we didn't have standing.
他们说我们没有立场。

715
00:50:10,938 --> 00:50:11,678
That's the other thing.
这就是另一件事。

716
00:50:12,239 --> 00:50:14,662
They said we didn't have standing, a technicality.
他们说我们没有立场，这是一个技术性问题。

717
00:50:14,882 --> 00:50:19,426
Can you imagine a system where a person in an election doesn't have standing?
你能想象一个系统，在选举中一个人没有立场吗？

718
00:50:19,466 --> 00:50:22,570
The President of the United States doesn't have standing.
美国总统没有立场。

719
00:50:22,910 --> 00:50:23,871
That's how we lost.
这就是我们失败的原因。

720
00:50:24,371 --> 00:50:27,775
If you look at the facts, and I'd love to have you do a special on it,
如果你看看事实，我很想让你做一个特别节目。

721
00:50:28,215 --> 00:50:36,000
I'll show you Georgia, and I'll show you Wisconsin, and I'll show you Pennsylvania, and I'll show you — we have so many facts and statistics.
我会给你展示乔治亚州，我会给你展示威斯康星州，我会给你展示宾夕法尼亚州，我会给你展示——我们有很多事实和统计数据。

722
00:50:36,281 --> 00:50:36,881
But you know what?
但你知道吗？

723
00:50:37,161 --> 00:50:40,723
That doesn't matter, because we have to solve the problem that we have right now.
这没关系，因为我们必须解决当前面临的问题。

724
00:50:40,784 --> 00:50:41,684
That's old news.
那是旧闻。

725
00:50:42,064 --> 00:50:48,989
And the problem that we have right now is we have a nation in decline, and they have put it into decline.
而我们现在面临的问题是，我们的国家正在衰退，而他们使其走向衰退。

726
00:50:49,329 --> 00:50:51,851
We have a nation that is dying, David.
我们有一个正在走向灭亡的国家，大卫。

727
00:50:51,991 --> 00:50:53,031
Mr. President, thank you.
总统先生，谢谢您。

728
00:50:53,432 --> 00:50:55,813
Vice President Harris, you heard the president there tonight.
哈里斯副总统，您今晚听到了总统的发言。

729
00:50:55,933 --> 00:50:57,713
He said he didn't say that, that he lost by a whisker.
他说他没有说过，他是以微弱的差距输掉的。

730
00:50:57,733 --> 00:51:04,396
So he still believes he did not lose the election that was won by President Biden and yourself.
所以他仍然相信他没有输掉由拜登总统和您赢得的选举。

731
00:51:05,136 --> 00:51:07,817
But I do want to ask you about something that's come up in the last couple of days.
但我确实想问您一些最近几天出现的事情。

732
00:51:07,837 --> 00:51:09,598
This was a post from President Trump.
这是特朗普总统的一条帖子。

733
00:51:10,218 --> 00:51:12,421
about this upcoming election just weeks away.
关于即将到来的选举，仅仅几周后。

734
00:51:12,461 --> 00:51:22,891
He said, when I win, those people who cheated, and then he lists donors, voters, election officials, he says, will be prosecuted to the fullest extent of the law, which will include long-term prison sentences.
他说，当我赢的时候，那些作弊的人，接着他列出了捐赠者、选民和选举官员，他说，他们将受到法律的最严厉制裁，包括长期监禁。

735
00:51:23,532 --> 00:51:27,416
One of your campaign's top lawyers responded, saying, we won't let Donald Trump intimidate us.
您竞选团队的一位首席律师回应说，我们不会让唐纳德·特朗普威胁我们。

736
00:51:27,776 --> 00:51:29,578
We won't let him suppress the vote.
我们不会让他压制投票。

737
00:51:30,078 --> 00:51:31,560
Is that what you believe he's trying to do here?
您认为他在这里试图这样做吗？

738
00:51:33,311 --> 00:51:36,094
Donald Trump was fired by 81 million people.
唐纳德·特朗普被8100万人民解雇了。

739
00:51:36,915 --> 00:51:38,256
So let's be clear about that.
所以我们要明确这一点。

740
00:51:38,577 --> 00:51:41,760
And clearly he is having a very difficult time processing that.
显然，他在处理这一点上非常困难。

741
00:51:42,714 --> 00:51:54,958
But we cannot afford to have a President of the United States who attempts, as he did in the past, to upend the will of the voters in a free and fair election.
但我们不能允许一个试图，如他过去所做的那样，颠覆自由公正选举中选民意志的美国总统。

742
00:51:55,738 --> 00:52:04,121
And I'm going to tell you that I have traveled the world as Vice President of the United States, and world leaders are laughing at Donald Trump.
我想告诉你，作为美国副总统，我已经走遍了世界，世界领导人正在嘲笑唐纳德·特朗普。

743
00:52:04,981 --> 00:52:10,443
I have talked with military leaders, some of whom worked with you, and they say you're a disgrace.
我与一些曾与您合作的军事领导人交谈过，他们说您是个耻辱。

744
00:52:11,703 --> 00:52:31,652
And when you then talk in this way in a presidential debate and deny what over and over again are court cases you have lost because you did in fact lose that election, it leads one to believe that perhaps we do not have in the candidate to my right the temperament
而当您在总统辩论中以这样的方式发言，并否认那些您因确实输掉选举而反复失利的法庭案件时，这让人相信，也许我们右侧的候选人缺乏

745
00:52:32,834 --> 00:52:37,418
or the ability to not be confused about fact.
或能力不被事实混淆。

746
00:52:37,959 --> 00:52:41,582
That's deeply troubling, and the American people deserve better.
这非常令人不安，而美国人民应得更好的。

747
00:52:42,463 --> 00:52:43,844
I'll give you one minute to respond, Mr. President.
我给您一分钟的时间回应，总统先生。

748
00:52:43,904 --> 00:52:45,265
Let me just tell you about world leaders.
让我告诉您一些关于世界领导人的事。

749
00:52:45,826 --> 00:52:48,128
Viktor Orban, one of the most respected men.
维克托·欧尔班，是最受尊敬的人之一。

750
00:52:48,328 --> 00:52:49,409
They call him a strong man.
他们称他为强人。

751
00:52:49,449 --> 00:52:50,770
He's a tough person.
他是一个强硬的人

752
00:52:51,551 --> 00:52:51,931
Smart.
聪明

753
00:52:52,472 --> 00:52:53,653
Prime Minister of Hungary.
匈牙利总理

754
00:52:54,173 --> 00:52:56,715
They said, why is the whole world blowing up?
他们说，为什么整个世界都在动荡？

755
00:52:56,795 --> 00:52:57,956
Three years ago, it wasn't.
三年前，情况并不是这样

756
00:52:58,016 --> 00:52:59,077
Why is it blowing up?
为什么会动荡？

757
00:52:59,778 --> 00:53:03,481
He said, because you need Trump back as president.
他说，因为你需要特朗普重新担任总统

758
00:53:04,022 --> 00:53:05,083
They were afraid of him.
他们害怕他

759
00:53:05,183 --> 00:53:06,264
China was afraid.
中国害怕

760
00:53:06,324 --> 00:53:08,746
And I don't like to use the word afraid, but I'm just quoting him.
我不喜欢用“害怕”这个词，但我只是引用他的话

761
00:53:09,286 --> 00:53:10,447
China was afraid of him.
中国害怕他

762
00:53:10,868 --> 00:53:12,469
North Korea was afraid of him.
朝鲜也害怕他

763
00:53:12,909 --> 00:53:14,971
Look at what's going on with North Korea, by the way.
顺便说一下，看看朝鲜发生了什么

764
00:53:15,291 --> 00:53:17,013
He said Russia was afraid of him.
他说俄罗斯也害怕他

765
00:53:17,393 --> 00:53:23,659
I ended the Nord Stream 2 pipeline and Biden put it back on day one, but he ended the XL pipeline.
我结束了北溪2号管道，而拜登在第一天就让它重新启用，但他却结束了XL管道

766
00:53:24,239 --> 00:53:33,908
The XL pipeline in our country, he ended that, but he let the Russians build a pipeline going all over Europe and heading into Germany, the biggest pipeline in the world.
在我们国家，他结束了XL管道，但却让俄罗斯建造了一条横贯整个欧洲并通往德国的管道，世界上最大的管道

767
00:53:34,288 --> 00:53:34,469
Look.
看看

768
00:53:35,430 --> 00:53:37,531
Victor Orban said it.
维克托·欧尔班说过

769
00:53:37,911 --> 00:53:42,192
He said the most respected, most feared person is Donald Trump.
他说，最受尊敬、最令人畏惧的人是唐纳德·特朗普

770
00:53:42,532 --> 00:53:45,253
We had no problems when Trump was president.
当特朗普担任总统时，我们没有任何问题

771
00:53:45,673 --> 00:53:53,835
But when this weak, pathetic man that you saw at a debate just a few months ago, that if he weren't in that debate, he'd be running instead of her.
但是当你在几个月前看到的那个软弱、可怜的人出现在辩论中时，如果他不在辩论中，他将会比她更有竞争力

772
00:53:53,875 --> 00:53:54,695
She got no votes.
她得不到任何选票

773
00:53:54,955 --> 00:53:56,315
He got 14 million votes.
他得到了1400万选票

774
00:53:56,355 --> 00:53:58,836
What you did, you talk about a threat to democracy.
你所做的，就是谈论对民主的威胁

775
00:53:59,376 --> 00:54:02,077
He got 14 million votes and they threw him out of office.
他得到了1400万选票，他们却把他赶出了办公室

776
00:54:02,737 --> 00:54:03,217
And you know what?
你知道吗？

777
00:54:03,237 --> 00:54:04,198
I'll give you a little secret.
我给你一个小秘密

778
00:54:04,258 --> 00:54:04,978
He hates her.
他恨她

779
00:54:05,259 --> 00:54:06,299
He can't stand her.
他无法忍受她

780
00:54:06,820 --> 00:54:08,541
But he got 14 million votes.
但他得到了1400万选票

781
00:54:08,901 --> 00:54:09,802
They threw him out.
他们把他赶了出去。

782
00:54:10,202 --> 00:54:11,543
She got zero votes.
她得了零票。

783
00:54:11,843 --> 00:54:16,005
And when she ran, she was the first one to leave because she failed.
当她参选时，她是第一个因为失败而退场的。

784
00:54:16,406 --> 00:54:17,406
And now she's running.
而现在她又在竞选。

785
00:54:17,747 --> 00:54:19,808
I don't understand it, but I'm okay with it because...
我不理解，但我对此无所谓，因为...

786
00:54:20,208 --> 00:54:20,628
Your time is up.
你的时间到了。

787
00:54:20,648 --> 00:54:20,828
Thank you.
谢谢。

788
00:54:20,848 --> 00:54:21,688
I think we're going to do very well.
我觉得我们会做得很好。

789
00:54:21,708 --> 00:54:22,809
We've got a lot more to get to.
我们还有很多事情要处理。

790
00:54:22,849 --> 00:54:28,230
Turning now to the Israel-Hamas war and the hostages who are still being held, Americans among them.
现在转向以色列-哈马斯战争，以及仍被扣为人质的情况，其中包括美国人。

791
00:54:28,590 --> 00:54:32,810
Vice President Harris, in December you said, quote, Israel has a right to defend itself.
哈里斯副总统，您在十二月曾说过，引用，   以色列有权自卫。

792
00:54:32,870 --> 00:54:38,331
But you added, quote, it matters how, saying international humanitarian law must be respected.
但您补充说，引用，   这要看如何做，必须尊重国际人道主义法。

793
00:54:38,511 --> 00:54:41,132
Israel must do more to protect innocent civilians.
以色列必须采取更多措施来保护无辜平民。

794
00:54:41,672 --> 00:54:43,132
You said that nine months ago.
您九个月前是这样说的。

795
00:54:43,212 --> 00:54:45,033
Now an estimated 40,000 Palestinians are dead.
现在估计已有四万名巴勒斯坦人死亡。

796
00:54:46,713 --> 00:54:48,914
Nearly 100 hostages remain.
近百名人质仍然被扣留。

797
00:54:49,314 --> 00:54:53,356
Just last week, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said there's not a deal in the making.
就在上周，内塔尼亚胡总理表示没有达成协议。

798
00:54:53,757 --> 00:54:56,458
President Biden has not been able to break through the stalemate.
拜登总统未能打破僵局。

799
00:54:56,798 --> 00:54:57,518
How would you do it?
您会如何做？

800
00:54:58,839 --> 00:55:00,920
Well, let's understand how we got here.
好吧，让我们了解一下我们是如何走到这一步的。

801
00:55:01,560 --> 00:55:06,503
On October 7, Hamas, a terrorist organization,
在十月七日，哈马斯，一个恐怖组织，   屠杀了1200名以色列人，许多都是仅仅参加音乐会的年轻人。

802
00:55:08,280 --> 00:55:14,446
slaughtered 1,200 Israelis, many of them young people who were simply attending a concert.
女性遭受到可怕的强奸。

803
00:55:15,207 --> 00:55:17,049
Women were horribly raped.
所以我绝对在那时说过，现在也说，以色列有权自卫。

804
00:55:17,589 --> 00:55:22,514
And so absolutely, I said then, I say now, Israel has a right to defend itself.
我们也会这样做。

805
00:55:22,574 --> 00:55:22,974
We would.
而且它如何自卫非常重要，因为同样也有太多无辜的巴勒斯坦人被杀。

806
00:55:24,326 --> 00:55:32,076
And how it does so matters, because it is also true far too many innocent Palestinians have been killed.
儿童，母亲。

807
00:55:32,918 --> 00:55:33,959
Children, mothers.
我们知道这场战争必须结束。

808
00:55:34,980 --> 00:55:38,445
What we know is that this war must end.
它必须立即结束，结束的方式是我们需要达成停火协议，并且需要释放人质。

809
00:55:39,326 --> 00:55:46,450
It must end immediately, and the way it will end is we need a ceasefire deal and we need the hostages out.
因此我们将继续不分昼夜地为此努力。

810
00:55:47,210 --> 00:55:50,372
And so we will continue to work around the clock on that.
我们将继续推动这一进程。

811
00:55:51,152 --> 00:55:56,715
Work around the clock also understanding that we must chart a course for a two-state solution.
我们必须全力以赴，同时理解我们必须为两国解决方案制定路线图

812
00:55:57,475 --> 00:56:05,563
And in that solution, there must be security for the Israeli people and Israel and an equal measure for the Palestinians.
在这个解决方案中，必须为以色列人民和以色列提供安全，同时也为巴勒斯坦人提供同等的保障

813
00:56:06,044 --> 00:56:19,398
But the one thing I will assure you always, I will always give Israel the ability to defend itself, in particular as it relates to Iran and any threat that Iran and its proxies pose to Israel.
但我可以向你们保证，我将始终给予以色列自我防卫的能力，特别是在与伊朗及其代理人对以色列构成威胁时

814
00:56:19,938 --> 00:56:30,444
But we must have a two-state solution where we can rebuild Gaza, where the Palestinians have security, self-determination, and the dignity they so rightly deserve.
但我们必须有一个两国解决方案，在那里我们可以重建加沙，巴勒斯坦人拥有安全、自决权和他们应得的尊严

815
00:56:31,344 --> 00:56:40,829
President Trump, how would you negotiate with Netanyahu and also Hamas in order to get the hostages out and prevent the killing of more innocent civilians in Gaza?
特朗普总统，您将如何与内塔尼亚胡以及哈马斯谈判，以解救人质并防止更多无辜平民在加沙被杀？

816
00:56:41,149 --> 00:56:43,471
If I were president, it would have never started.
如果我是总统，这一切根本不会发生

817
00:56:43,991 --> 00:56:57,122
If I were president, Russia would have never, ever, I know Putin very well, he would have never, and there was no threat of it either, by the way, for four years, have gone into Ukraine and killed millions of people when you add it up.
如果我是总统，俄罗斯绝不会，我非常了解普京，他绝对不会，而且在过去四年里也没有任何威胁，进入乌克兰并造成数百万人的死亡

818
00:56:57,402 --> 00:56:59,784
Far worse than people understand what's going on over there.
情况远比人们理解的要糟糕得多

819
00:57:00,805 --> 00:57:05,070
But when she mentions about Israel, all of a sudden, she hates Israel.
但当她提到以色列时，突然间，她就讨厌以色列

820
00:57:05,371 --> 00:57:10,797
She wouldn't even meet with Netanyahu when he went to Congress to make a very important speech.
当内塔尼亚胡来到国会发表重要演讲时，她甚至不愿与他见面

821
00:57:11,078 --> 00:57:14,342
She refused to be there because she was at a sorority party of hers.
她拒绝出席，因为她在参加她的姐妹会聚会

822
00:57:14,662 --> 00:57:16,164
She wanted to go to the sorority party.
她想去姐妹会聚会

823
00:57:17,125 --> 00:57:18,085
She hates Israel.
她讨厌以色列

824
00:57:18,545 --> 00:57:23,487
If she's president, I believe that Israel will not exist within two years from now.
如果她成为总统，我相信以色列将在两年内不复存在

825
00:57:23,527 --> 00:57:26,408
And I've been pretty good at predictions, and I hope I'm wrong about that one.
我在预测方面一直表现不错，我希望我在这一点上是错的

826
00:57:27,088 --> 00:57:28,028
She hates Israel.
她讨厌以色列

827
00:57:28,388 --> 00:57:36,890
At the same time, in her own way, she hates the Arab population, because the whole place is going to get blown up.
与此同时，以她自己的方式，她也讨厌阿拉伯人，因为整个地方将会被摧毁

828
00:57:37,431 --> 00:57:40,411
Arabs, Jewish people, Israel.
阿拉伯人、犹太人、以色列

829
00:57:40,732 --> 00:57:41,712
Israel will be gone.
以色列将会消失

830
00:57:42,552 --> 00:57:44,094
It would have never happened.
这一切根本不会发生

831
00:57:44,334 --> 00:57:46,536
Iran was broke under Donald Trump.
在唐纳德·特朗普执政期间，伊朗是破产的

832
00:57:46,976 --> 00:57:51,901
Now Iran has $300 billion because they took off all the sanctions that I had.
现在伊朗有了3000亿美元，因为他们解除我施加的所有制裁

833
00:57:52,301 --> 00:57:59,308
Iran had no money for Hamas or Hezbollah or any of the 28 different spheres of terror.
伊朗没有钱给哈马斯或真主党，或任何28个不同的恐怖领域

834
00:57:59,488 --> 00:58:02,069
And they are spheres of terror, horrible terror.
而且它们确实是恐怖领域，糟糕的恐怖

835
00:58:02,450 --> 00:58:03,150
They had no money.
他们没有钱

836
00:58:03,530 --> 00:58:05,091
It was a big story, and you know it.
这是一个大新闻，你知道的

837
00:58:05,131 --> 00:58:06,712
You covered it very well, actually.
实际上，你们报道得很好

838
00:58:07,112 --> 00:58:09,213
They had no money for terror.
他们没有钱用于恐怖活动

839
00:58:09,653 --> 00:58:10,654
They were broke.
他们是破产的

840
00:58:11,074 --> 00:58:12,495
Now they're a rich nation.
现在他们是一个富裕的国家

841
00:58:12,735 --> 00:58:15,977
And now what they're doing is they're spreading that money around.
他们现在所做的就是把那些钱分散出去。

842
00:58:17,017 --> 00:58:20,020
Look at what's happening with the Houthis and Yemen.
看看胡塞武装和也门的局势。

843
00:58:20,320 --> 00:58:22,082
Look at what's going on in the Middle East.
看看中东发生的事情。

844
00:58:22,542 --> 00:58:23,884
This would have never happened.
这一切是绝对不会发生的。

845
00:58:24,164 --> 00:58:29,469
I will get that settled and fast, and I'll get the war with Ukraine and Russia ended.
我会迅速解决这个问题，并结束乌克兰与俄罗斯的战争。

846
00:58:30,089 --> 00:58:34,794
If I'm president-elect, I'll get it done before even becoming president.
如果我当选总统，我会在上任之前就完成这件事。

847
00:58:35,074 --> 00:58:37,297
Vice President Harris, he says you hate Israel.
哈里斯副总统，他说你讨厌以色列。

848
00:58:38,098 --> 00:58:39,700
That's absolutely not true.
这绝对不是真的。

849
00:58:39,720 --> 00:58:45,026
I have my entire career and life supported Israel and the Israeli people.
我在整个职业生涯和生活中都支持以色列和以色列人民。

850
00:58:45,427 --> 00:58:46,108
He knows that.
他知道这一点。

851
00:58:46,548 --> 00:58:49,993
He's trying to again divide and distract
他又在试图分裂和转移注意力

852
00:58:50,353 --> 00:58:58,858
from the reality, which is it is very well known that Donald Trump is weak and wrong on national security and foreign policy.
以掩盖事实，众所周知，唐纳德·特朗普在国家安全和外交政策上是软弱和错误的。

853
00:58:59,018 --> 00:59:05,702
It is well known that he admires dictators, wants to be a dictator on day one according to himself.
众所周知，他崇拜独裁者，自己也想在第一天就成为独裁者。

854
00:59:06,602 --> 00:59:14,965
It is well known that he said of Putin that he can do whatever the hell he wants and go into Ukraine.
众所周知，他曾说普京可以随心所欲地进入乌克兰。

855
00:59:15,605 --> 00:59:20,867
It is well known that he said when Russia went into Ukraine, it was brilliant.
众所周知，他曾说俄罗斯进入乌克兰时，这真是太聪明了。

856
00:59:21,867 --> 00:59:26,230
It is well known he exchanged love letters with Kim Jong-un.
众所周知，他和金正恩互换了情书。

857
00:59:27,191 --> 00:59:40,681
And it is absolutely well known that these dictators and autocrats are rooting for you to be president again, because they're so clear they can manipulate you with flattery and favors.
而且绝对众所周知，这些独裁者和专制者希望你再次成为总统，因为他们清楚可以用奉承和恩惠来操控你。

858
00:59:41,422 --> 00:59:42,543
And that is why
这就是为什么

859
00:59:43,869 --> 00:59:49,172
So many military leaders who you have worked with have told me you are a disgrace.
你曾合作过的许多军事领导人告诉我你是个耻辱。

860
00:59:49,952 --> 01:00:03,880
That is why we understand that we have to have a president who is not consistently weak and wrong on national security, including the importance of upholding and respecting in highest regard our military.
这就是为什么我们明白，我们需要一位在国家安全问题上不是一贯软弱和错误的总统，尤其是要高度重视和尊重我们的军队。

861
01:00:04,040 --> 01:00:05,321
Vice President Harris, thank you.
哈里斯副总统，谢谢。

862
01:00:06,582 --> 01:00:08,484
And she's the one that caused it.
而她就是导致这一切的人。

863
01:00:08,904 --> 01:00:18,315
That's weak on national security by allowing every nation last month for the year 168 different countries sending people into our country.
这在国家安全上是软弱的，允许去年168个不同国家的人进入我们的国家。

864
01:00:18,575 --> 01:00:19,977
Their crime weights are way down.
他们的犯罪率大幅下降。

865
01:00:20,918 --> 01:00:24,882
Putin endorsed her last week said I hope she wins and I think he meant it.
普京上周支持她说我希望她赢，我认为他是认真的。

866
01:00:25,583 --> 01:00:28,886
because what he's gotten away with is absolutely incredible.
因为他所逃避的事情绝对令人难以置信。

867
01:00:28,926 --> 01:00:30,187
It wouldn't have happened with me.
在我这里是不会发生的。

868
01:00:30,827 --> 01:00:35,851
The leaders of other countries think that they're weak and incompetent, and they are.
其他国家的领导人认为他们软弱无能，确实如此。

869
01:00:36,212 --> 01:00:37,633
They're grossly incompetent.
他们极其无能。

870
01:00:37,993 --> 01:00:39,494
And I just ask one question.
我只问一个问题。

871
01:00:39,875 --> 01:00:50,964
Why does Biden go in and kill the Keystone pipeline and approve the single biggest deal that Russia's ever made, Nord Stream 2, the biggest pipeline anywhere in the world going to Germany and all over Europe?
为什么拜登要关闭基斯通管道，却批准俄罗斯有史以来最大的交易——诺德斯特里姆2号，这是通往德国和整个欧洲的最大管道？

872
01:00:51,604 --> 01:00:53,746
because they're weak and they're ineffective.
因为他们软弱无能。

873
01:00:54,106 --> 01:00:56,308
And Biden, by the way, gets paid a lot of money.
顺便提一句，拜登赚了很多钱。

874
01:00:56,328 --> 01:00:56,668
Thank you.
谢谢。

875
01:00:56,708 --> 01:00:58,150
We have a lot of issues to get to.
我们有很多问题需要讨论。

876
01:00:58,310 --> 01:01:04,535
We'll be right back with much more of this historic ABC News presidential debate from the National Constitution Center right here in Philadelphia.
我们将在费城的国家宪法中心继续这场历史性的ABC新闻总统辩论，稍后回来。

877
01:01:04,635 --> 01:01:05,196
Back in a moment.
稍后回来。

878
01:01:06,497 --> 01:01:09,599
The ABC News presidential debate will continue after this.
ABC新闻总统辩论将在此之后继续。

879
01:01:17,742 --> 01:01:21,485
from the National Constitution Center in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania.
来自宾夕法尼亚州费城的国家宪法中心。

880
01:01:22,205 --> 01:01:25,388
Here again, David Muir and Lindsay Davis.
再次欢迎大卫·穆尔和林赛·戴维斯。

881
01:01:25,988 --> 01:01:29,051
Welcome back to this historic ABC News presidential debate tonight.
欢迎回到今晚这场历史性的ABC新闻总统辩论。

882
01:01:29,071 --> 01:01:31,413
We're going to continue here, and I want to turn to the war in Ukraine.
我们将继续进行，我想转向乌克兰战争。

883
01:01:31,433 --> 01:01:33,895
We're now two and a half years into this conflict.
我们现在已经进入这场冲突两年半。

884
01:01:33,935 --> 01:01:45,844
Mr. President, it has been the position of the Biden administration that we must defend Ukraine from Russia, from Vladimir Putin, to defend their sovereignty, their democracy, that it's in America's best interest to do so, arguing that if Putin wins,
总统先生，拜登政府的立场是，我们必须保护乌克兰免受俄罗斯和普京的侵害，以维护他们的主权和民主，这符合美国的最佳利益，认为如果普京获胜，

885
01:01:46,244 --> 01:01:48,886
He may be emboldened to move even further into other countries.
他可能会更加肆无忌惮地向其他国家扩张。

886
01:01:49,506 --> 01:01:51,868
You have said you would solve this war in 24 hours.
您曾说过，您会在24小时内解决这场战争。

887
01:01:51,908 --> 01:01:53,629
You said so just before the break tonight.
您今晚在休息前刚说过这个。

888
01:01:54,030 --> 01:01:55,811
How exactly would you do that?
您到底会如何做到这一点？

889
01:01:56,091 --> 01:01:57,812
And I want to ask you a very simple question tonight.
我今晚想问您一个非常简单的问题。

890
01:01:58,092 --> 01:02:00,414
Do you want Ukraine to win this war?
您希望乌克兰赢得这场战争吗？

891
01:02:01,034 --> 01:02:02,255
I want the war to stop.
我希望战争停止。

892
01:02:02,576 --> 01:02:08,239
I want to save lives that are being uselessly people being killed by the millions.
我想拯救那些毫无意义地被杀死的生命，数以百万计。

893
01:02:08,320 --> 01:02:09,160
It's the millions.
这是数以百万计。

894
01:02:09,560 --> 01:02:13,143
It's so much worse than the numbers that you're getting, which are fake numbers.
这比您得到的数字要糟糕得多，那些都是假数字。

895
01:02:13,823 --> 01:02:14,004
Look,
听着，

896
01:02:15,069 --> 01:02:24,273
We're in for 250 billion or more because they don't ask Europe, which is a much bigger beneficiary to getting this thing done than we are.
我们已经投入了2500亿美元或更多，因为他们没有要求欧洲，欧洲是获得这项交易的更大受益者。

897
01:02:25,154 --> 01:02:33,838
They're in for 150 billion dollars less because Biden and you don't have the courage to ask Europe like I did with NATO.
他们少投入了1500亿美元，因为拜登和您没有勇气像我对待北约时那样要求欧洲。

898
01:02:34,278 --> 01:02:38,220
They paid billions and billions, hundreds of billions of dollars when I said
当我说，

899
01:02:38,820 --> 01:02:41,441
Either you pay up, or we're not going to protect you anymore.
要么你们支付，要么我们就不再保护你们时，他们支付了数十亿、数百亿美元。

900
01:02:41,501 --> 01:02:45,363
So that's maybe one of the reasons they don't like me as much as they like weak people.
所以这也许是他们不喜欢我而更喜欢软弱之人的原因之一。

901
01:02:45,843 --> 01:02:48,365
But you take a look at what's happening.
但你看看发生了什么。

902
01:02:48,685 --> 01:02:52,126
We're in for $250 to $275 billion.
我们面临着2500亿到2750亿美元的损失。

903
01:02:52,406 --> 01:02:53,767
They're into $100 to $150.
他们面临着100亿到150亿美元的损失。

904
01:02:55,248 --> 01:02:57,789
They should be forced to equalize.
他们应该被迫达到平衡。

905
01:02:58,089 --> 01:03:00,770
With that being said, I want to get the war settled.
话虽如此，我想解决战争问题。

906
01:03:00,990 --> 01:03:03,652
I know Zelensky very well, and I know Putin very well.
我非常了解泽伦斯基，也非常了解普京。

907
01:03:03,692 --> 01:03:05,893
I have a good relationship, and they respect
我与他们关系良好，他们尊重

908
01:03:06,733 --> 01:03:07,974
your president, okay?
你的总统，好吗？

909
01:03:08,014 --> 01:03:08,935
They respect me.
他们尊重我。

910
01:03:08,975 --> 01:03:10,156
They don't respect Biden.
他们不尊重拜登。

911
01:03:10,216 --> 01:03:11,277
How would you respect him?
你怎么会尊重他呢？

912
01:03:11,557 --> 01:03:11,897
Why?
Why?

913
01:03:11,937 --> 01:03:12,638
For what reason?
出于什么理由？

914
01:03:12,998 --> 01:03:17,001
He hasn't even made a phone call in two years to Putin, hasn't spoken to anybody.
他在两年内甚至没有给普京打过一个电话，没和任何人交谈过。

915
01:03:17,301 --> 01:03:18,462
They don't even try and get it.
他们甚至都没有尝试去解决这个问题。

916
01:03:18,782 --> 01:03:21,104
That is a war that's dying to be settled.
这是一场急需解决的战争。

917
01:03:21,424 --> 01:03:24,046
I will get it settled before I even become president.
我会在成为总统之前解决这个问题。

918
01:03:24,086 --> 01:03:31,232
If I win, when I'm president-elect, and what I'll do is I'll speak to one, I'll speak to the other, I'll get them together.
如果我赢了，当我成为当选总统时，我会和其中一个谈，和另一个谈，我会让他们聚在一起。

919
01:03:31,512 --> 01:03:33,213
That war would have never happened.
这场战争本来不会发生。

920
01:03:33,554 --> 01:03:36,236
And in fact, when I saw Putin after I left,
事实上，当我离开后见到普京时，

921
01:03:36,816 --> 01:03:40,197
Unfortunately, left because our country has gone to hell.
不幸的是，我离开是因为我们的国家已经糟糕透顶。

922
01:03:40,697 --> 01:03:44,478
But after I left, when I saw him building up soldiers, he did it after I left.
但在我离开后，当我看到他在集结士兵时，他是在我离开后才这么做的。

923
01:03:45,118 --> 01:03:47,739
I said, oh, he must be negotiating.
我说，哦，他一定在谈判。

924
01:03:47,819 --> 01:03:49,980
It must be a good, strong point of negotiation.
这一定是一个良好的、强有力的谈判时机。

925
01:03:50,320 --> 01:03:54,121
Well, it wasn't because Biden had no idea how to talk to him.
结果并不是这样，因为拜登根本不知道怎么和他谈。

926
01:03:54,361 --> 01:03:56,121
He had no idea how to stop it.
他根本不知道怎么阻止这一切。

927
01:03:56,421 --> 01:03:59,702
And now you have millions of people dead and it's only getting worse.
现在你有数百万人死去，情况只在恶化。

928
01:03:59,782 --> 01:04:01,463
And it could lead to World War Three.
这可能导致第三次世界大战。

929
01:04:01,723 --> 01:04:02,783
Don't kid yourself, David.
别自欺欺人，戴维。

930
01:04:03,223 --> 01:04:08,826
We're playing with World War III, and we have a president that we don't even know if he's—where is our president?
我们正在玩弄第三次世界大战，而我们有一个总统，我们甚至不知道他——我们的总统在哪里？

931
01:04:09,106 --> 01:04:10,587
We don't even know if he's a president.
我们甚至不知道他是否是总统

932
01:04:10,607 --> 01:04:13,629
And just to clarify here— They threw him out of a campaign like a dog.
为了澄清一下——他们像扔狗一样把他从竞选中赶了出去

933
01:04:13,669 --> 01:04:14,389
We don't even know.
我们甚至不知道

934
01:04:14,830 --> 01:04:15,750
Is he our president?
他是我们的总统吗

935
01:04:16,070 --> 01:04:19,072
But we have a president— Mr. President— —that doesn't know he's alive.
但我们有一位总统——总统先生——他甚至不知道自己还活着

936
01:04:19,352 --> 01:04:19,973
Your time is up.
你的时间到了

937
01:04:20,773 --> 01:04:22,054
Just to clarify the question.
只是为了澄清这个问题

938
01:04:22,694 --> 01:04:23,975
Do you believe it's in the U.S.
你认为乌克兰赢得这场战争对美国

939
01:04:24,075 --> 01:04:26,578
best interest for Ukraine to win this war, yes or no?
的最佳利益是，是还是不是

940
01:04:26,598 --> 01:04:27,458
I think it's the U.S.
我认为这是美国

941
01:04:27,538 --> 01:04:30,681
best interest to get this war finished and just get it done.
的最佳利益，尽快结束这场战争

942
01:04:31,122 --> 01:04:32,082
Negotiate a deal.
谈判达成协议

943
01:04:32,323 --> 01:04:37,007
Because we have to stop all of these human lives from being destroyed.
因为我们必须阻止所有这些生命被摧毁

944
01:04:37,027 --> 01:04:38,628
I want to take this to Vice President Harris.
我想把这个问题抛给副总统哈里斯

945
01:04:38,648 --> 01:04:42,331
I want to get your thoughts on support for Ukraine in this moment.
我想听听你对当前支持乌克兰的看法

946
01:04:42,612 --> 01:04:47,036
But also, as Commander-in-Chief, if elected, how would you deal with Vladimir Putin?
但作为指挥官，如果当选，你将如何应对弗拉基米尔·普京？

947
01:04:47,116 --> 01:04:49,598
And would it be any different from what we're seeing from President Biden?
这会有什么不同于我们看到的拜登总统的做法吗？

948
01:04:50,680 --> 01:04:56,200
Well, first of all, it's important to remind the former president you're not running against Joe Biden, you're running against me.
首先，重要的是要提醒前总统，你不是在与乔·拜登竞选，你是在与我竞争

949
01:04:58,323 --> 01:05:04,266
I believe the reason that Donald Trump says that this war would be over within 24 hours is because he would just give it up.
我相信唐纳德·特朗普说这场战争将在24小时内结束的原因，是因为他会选择放弃

950
01:05:05,166 --> 01:05:06,927
And that's not who we are as Americans.
这不是我们作为美国人的本色

951
01:05:06,967 --> 01:05:08,428
Let's understand what happened here.
让我们了解这里发生了什么

952
01:05:09,268 --> 01:05:26,497
I actually met with Zelensky a few days before Russia invaded, tried through force to change territorial boundaries, to defy one of the most important international rules and norms, which is the importance of sovereignty and territorial integrity.
在俄罗斯入侵之前的几天，我实际上与泽连斯基会面，试图通过武力改变领土边界，挑战国际上最重要的规则和规范之一，即主权和领土完整的重要性

953
01:05:27,037 --> 01:05:28,598
And I met with President Zelensky.
我与泽连斯基总统会面

954
01:05:28,738 --> 01:05:32,441
I shared with him American intelligence about how he could defend himself.
我向他分享了有关他如何自我防卫的美国情报

955
01:05:33,002 --> 01:05:37,265
Days later, I went to NATO's eastern flank, to Poland and Romania.
几天后，我前往北约的东翼，波兰和罗马尼亚

956
01:05:38,086 --> 01:05:45,572
And through the work that I and others did, we brought 50 countries together to support Ukraine in its righteous defense.
通过我和其他人的努力，我们将50个国家聚集在一起，支持乌克兰进行正义的防卫

957
01:05:46,232 --> 01:05:59,425
And because of our support, because of the air defense, the ammunition, the artillery, the Javelins, the Abrams tanks that we have provided, Ukraine stands as an independent and free country.
因为我们的支持，因为空中防御、弹药、炮兵、标枪导弹、我们提供的艾布拉姆斯坦克，乌克兰作为一个独立和自由的国家屹立不倒

958
01:05:59,665 --> 01:06:03,128
If Donald Trump were president, Putin would be sitting in Kiev right now.
如果唐纳德·特朗普是总统，普京现在就会坐在基辅

959
01:06:03,869 --> 01:06:09,332
And understand what that would mean, because Putin's agenda is not just about Ukraine.
要理解这意味着什么，因为普京的议程不仅仅是关于乌克兰

960
01:06:10,132 --> 01:06:24,380
Understand why the European allies and our NATO allies are so thankful that you are no longer president, and that we understand the importance of the greatest military alliance the world has ever known, which is NATO.
要理解为什么欧洲盟友和我们的北约盟友如此感激你不再是总统，以及我们理解世界上最大的军事联盟——北约的重要性

961
01:06:25,200 --> 01:06:31,964
and what we have done to preserve the ability of Zelensky and the Ukrainians to fight for their independence.
我们所做的就是保留泽连斯基和乌克兰人民为争取独立而战的能力。

962
01:06:32,425 --> 01:06:38,728
Otherwise, Putin would be sitting in Kiev with his eyes on the rest of Europe, starting with Poland.
否则，普京会坐在基辅，目光瞄准整个欧洲，从波兰开始。

963
01:06:38,788 --> 01:06:53,618
And why don't you tell the 800,000 Polish-Americans right here in Pennsylvania how quickly you would give up for the sake of favor and what you think is a friendship with what is known to be a dictator who would eat you for lunch.
你为什么不告诉在宾夕法尼亚的80万波兰裔美国人，你会多快为了所谓的友谊而放弃，和一个众所周知的会把你吃掉的独裁者交朋友？

964
01:06:55,182 --> 01:06:56,283
Vice President Harris, thank you.
哈里斯副总统，谢谢你。

965
01:06:56,303 --> 01:06:58,083
We've heard from both of you on Ukraine tonight.
今晚我们听到了你们两位关于乌克兰的看法。

966
01:06:58,284 --> 01:06:59,984
Afghanistan came up in the last hour.
阿富汗在刚才的一个小时内被提及。

967
01:07:00,004 --> 01:07:02,546
I wanted her to respond to something you said earlier.
我想让她回应你之前说的某些话。

968
01:07:03,586 --> 01:07:05,007
Please, I'll give you a minute here.
请，我给你一分钟时间。

969
01:07:06,229 --> 01:07:13,813
Putin would be sitting in Moscow, and he wouldn't have lost 300,000 men and women, but he would have been sitting in Moscow.
普京会坐在莫斯科，他不会损失30万的男女，但他会坐在莫斯科。

970
01:07:14,254 --> 01:07:14,954
Quiet, please.
请安静。

971
01:07:15,554 --> 01:07:19,997
He would have been sitting in Moscow much happier than he is right now.
他会比现在更开心地坐在莫斯科。

972
01:07:20,717 --> 01:07:23,939
But eventually, you know, he's got a thing that other people don't have.
但最终，你知道，他拥有其他人所没有的东西。

973
01:07:23,959 --> 01:07:24,980
He's got nuclear weapons.
他拥有核武器。

974
01:07:25,000 --> 01:07:26,160
They don't ever talk about that.
他们从来没有谈论过这个。

975
01:07:26,180 --> 01:07:27,321
He's got nuclear weapons.
他拥有核武器。

976
01:07:27,741 --> 01:07:28,922
Nobody ever thinks about that.
没有人会想到这一点。

977
01:07:29,522 --> 01:07:33,945
And eventually, maybe he'll use them, and maybe he hasn't been that threatening.
最终，也许他会使用它们，也许他并没有那么具威胁性。

978
01:07:34,545 --> 01:07:37,966
But he does have that, something we don't even like to talk about.
但他确实拥有这个，我们甚至不愿意谈论。

979
01:07:38,147 --> 01:07:39,447
Nobody likes to talk about it.
没有人愿意谈论这个。

980
01:07:39,867 --> 01:07:44,829
But just so you understand, they sent her to negotiate peace before this war started.
但你要明白，他们在这场战争开始前派她去谈判和平。

981
01:07:45,209 --> 01:07:51,792
Three days later, he went in and he started the war because everything they said was weak and stupid.
三天后，他进攻并发动了战争，因为他们所说的一切都软弱无力和愚蠢。

982
01:07:52,112 --> 01:07:53,373
They said the wrong things.
他们说错了话。

983
01:07:53,613 --> 01:07:55,173
That war should have never started.
那场战争根本不该开始。

984
01:07:55,494 --> 01:07:56,674
She was the emissary.
她是特使。

985
01:07:56,974 --> 01:08:00,936
They sent her in to negotiate with Zelensky and Putin.
他们派她去与泽连斯基和普京谈判。

986
01:08:01,636 --> 01:08:02,276
And she did.
而她确实去做了。

987
01:08:02,717 --> 01:08:04,398
And the war started three days later.
三天后战争就开始了。

988
01:08:04,778 --> 01:08:06,919
And that's the kind of talent we have with her.
这就是我们拥有的她的才能。

989
01:08:07,259 --> 01:08:09,241
She's worse than Biden, in my opinion.
在我看来，她比拜登还糟。

990
01:08:09,281 --> 01:08:11,642
I think he's the worst president in the history of our country.
我认为他是我们国家历史上最差的总统。

991
01:08:12,022 --> 01:08:15,685
She goes down as the worst vice president in the history of our country.
她将被记住为我们国家历史上最差的副总统。

992
01:08:15,725 --> 01:08:16,745
But let me tell you something.
但让我告诉你一件事。

993
01:08:17,225 --> 01:08:19,427
She is a horrible negotiator.
她是个糟糕的谈判者。

994
01:08:19,927 --> 01:08:21,608
They sent her in to negotiate.
他们派她去谈判。

995
01:08:21,868 --> 01:08:24,550
As soon as they left, Putin did the invasion.
一离开，普京就发动了入侵。

996
01:08:24,790 --> 01:08:25,571
President Trump, thank you.
特朗普总统，谢谢您。

997
01:08:25,591 --> 01:08:26,392
You did bring up something.
您确实提到了某些事情。

998
01:08:26,512 --> 01:08:28,354
You said she went to negotiate with Vladimir Putin.
您说她去与弗拉基米尔·普京谈判。

999
01:08:28,374 --> 01:08:30,637
Vice President Harris, have you ever met Vladimir Putin?
哈里斯副总统，您见过弗拉基米尔·普京吗？

1000
01:08:30,657 --> 01:08:31,619
Can you clarify tonight?
今晚您能澄清一下吗？

1001
01:08:32,359 --> 01:08:35,984
Yet again, I said at the beginning of this debate, you're going to hear a bunch of lies coming from this fellow.
我在这场辩论开始时就说过，您将听到这个家伙说的一堆谎言。

1002
01:08:36,525 --> 01:08:37,326
And that is another one.
这又是一个谎言。

1003
01:08:38,287 --> 01:08:42,052
When I went to meet with President Zelensky, I've now met with him over five times.
当我去见泽伦斯基总统时，我现在已经见过他超过五次。

1004
01:08:43,345 --> 01:09:05,650
The reality is it has been about standing as America always should, as a leader upholding international rules and norms, as a leader who shows strength, understanding that the alliances we have around the world are dependent on our ability to look out for our friends and not favor
